me personally, every single one of these

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:39.320
standards came from specific moments in

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.800
my life when I was being the complete

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:43.480
opposite and being cheap with my time

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:46.320
and with my energy, my attention and

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:48.920
with myself. Standard one, I stopped

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:50.600
explaining myself. Marcus Aurelius was

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:53.080
the emperor of Rome. At the time, he was

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:55.040
the most powerful man on the planet and

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:57.320
as the emperor, he would also keep

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:59.080
ba-da-bing a private journal that was

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:00.800
never meant to be read by anyone. Well,

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:02.200
obviously someone did, I did. But

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:03.640
throughout his life, he didn't feel like

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:05.840
he had to go around explaining his

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:08.280
philosophy to people who didn't ask. He

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:10.040
didn't have to justify anything and he

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:12.680
built what the Stoics call an inner

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:14.840
citadel, a private interior life that

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:17.840
you don't get access to [music] unless

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:20.280
he specifically lets you in. Meanwhile,

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.920
I was out here writing paragraphs on

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:23.600
group chats explaining why I couldn't

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.280
come to brunch and I swear nobody said

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:27.000
