with your energy, you're going to be

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:43.640
broke. And we always pay for something

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:45.240
in life, no matter what we do. So, when

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:47.040
we finally meet someone who deserves

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:49.480
that, you don't have any of yourself

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:51.480
left. This is why radical self-attention

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:53.800
is so important. You got to build

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:55.840
yourself up first. If not, you just

00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:57.200
spend all your energy onto other people

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:59.720
who don't even know how to say thank

00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:01.120
you. Epictetus was a former Stoic, and

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:03.240
he's been through a lot because he was

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:05.600
also a former slave. He said, "Make the

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:07.400
best use of what is in your power, and

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:09.360
take the [music] rest as it happens." In

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:10.880
my life, it looked like I was the girl

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:12.680
who was always making plans, talking

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:14.600
first, giving 10 chances to people who

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:16.560
honestly didn't even deserve a second

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:18.640
chance. And I would be proud of that.

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:20.880
I'd look at me, I'm so loyal and I care

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:22.600
so much. But I was chasing constantly

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:24.320
because being still felt so weird to me.

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:27.600
We need to discipline ourselves a bit

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:29.480
and always be ready to walk away from

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:31.920
anything. Even if we give something our

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:33.280
all, if it doesn't meet you at the same

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:35.640
place where you're at, you better be

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:37.680
willing to walk away. That is just

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:39.000
self-respect. If you keep giving and

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:40.880
giving up to a certain point, you're

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:42.800
going to have nothing. So, the standard

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:45.000
is, if I'm the only one reaching, I will

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:47.400
release and just think, "Well, I guess I

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:49.920
won't bother." Then quietly redirect

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:52.000
that energy towards whatever is actually

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:53.520
worth showing up for. You actually don't

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:55.640
lose anyone when you stop chasing them.

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:57.440
And remember, the world always works in

00:10:55.640 --> 00:10:59.560
ironies and paradoxes. That's just how

00:10:57.440 --> 00:11:01.040
it is. It's a constant push and pull.

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:03.000
And if you're the one pushing, then

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:05.520
someone is pulling away from you. If you

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:08.400
just let go and let it happen, [music]

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:10.320
truly your life will be rearranged. You

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:12.680
have to be more precious about yourself

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:14.480
so that you can give your best to people

00:11:12.680 --> 00:11:16.560
who are there to give you the same type

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:18.040
of value instead of just being drained

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:20.160
by everyone and having nothing left.

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:22.000
Standard number four, choose to do hard

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:24.120
things. Seneca, another Stoic

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:26.200
philosopher, used to sleep on a hard

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:28.560
floor about once a month as proof that

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:30.720
comfort doesn't own him. He would eat

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:33.080
the most boring food and deliberately

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:35.800
practice poverty so that if he ever lost

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:38.160
anything, he knew exactly how to deal

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:41.160
with that. That's voluntary discomfort.

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:43.280
For me, I didn't have to sleep on floors

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:45.200
to learn that. I just choose to do hard

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:47.600
things on my own time because I used to

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:50.200
wait until things got so unbearable

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:52.280
before I act on it. For example, the job

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:53.640
had to make me so physically ill, I

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:56.680
wouldn't even quit. They would have to

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:57.920
fire me or my body forces me to rest

00:11:56.680 --> 00:12:00.400
because I wouldn't want to rest

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:03.160
otherwise. So, I was the queen of it's

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:05.960
not that bad until you're almost dead,

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:08.120
basically. If it truly was that bad and

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:09.840
even worse, then I do not have the

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:12.000
energy at that point to deal with that.

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:14.000
And trust me, that is always the worst

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:16.960
option for you. So, if you choose to do

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:18.920
hard things now, no one has to force you

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:21.760
into it and you will actually have more

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:23.240
capacity than when you have no choice at

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:25.840
all. It's better for you to have a

00:12:23.240 --> 00:12:27.880
choice every time, especially if you do

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:29.880
these things and you succeed, then your

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:31.280
body and your mind will learn to trust

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:32.840
you more. You can't even carry yourself

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:34.360
better physically. And when you can

00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:36.520
trust yourself to do the necessary

00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:38.520
things for yourself, you will develop

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:41.280
more self-confidence and you become a

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:43.000
safe person for yourself. So, whenever

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:45.200
I'm feeling defensive or controlling

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:47.560
about something, I will step back and

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:49.880
examine where it's coming from before I

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:52.200
even react to it. Whether it's someone

00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:54.000
unintentionally triggering a deep-seated

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:55.720
insecurity in me that I have or

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:57.600
something like that, I have learned that

00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:59.360
it's not my job to change someone else's

00:12:57.600 --> 00:13:00.920
mind about their beliefs. Their life is

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:02.680
their responsibility, so I'm not

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:04.680
responsible for that, but I can also

00:13:02.680 --> 00:13:07.040
work on my own insecurity so that I

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:09.040
don't get triggered so easily or lash

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:11.080
out at someone who didn't even deserve

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:12.360
it. It's very important for me to notice

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:13.839
this distinction today because

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:15.640
unfortunately, one of the things that

00:13:13.839 --> 00:13:17.280
comes with being highly visible online

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:19.440
is that people lash out at me all the

00:13:17.280 --> 00:13:21.400
time randomly over something that I say

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:23.680
or maybe I had an opinion that offended

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:25.040
them, so they crash out in the comment

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:26.160
section or they send me an angry email,

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:28.360
whatever it is, they have to take

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:30.640
responsibility for themselves. So, if

00:13:28.360 --> 00:13:32.160
anyone has a negative opinion about you

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:33.800
or has the wrong idea about something,

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:35.960
the only thing you can control is your

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:37.320
own narrative. Not everyone is going to

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:39.440
like you. That's just a fact. If

00:13:37.320 --> 00:13:41.760
anything, they only have a very limited

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:44.240
scope of who you are based on how they

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:45.600
perceive you, which is all about them.

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:47.240
So, it's actually ridiculous when

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:49.040
someone takes something that you say

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:50.400
very personally, especially if it's not

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:52.000
meant to be an attack or anything,

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:53.560
because for me, I know I don't deserve

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:55.160
any of this. Another hard thing to do is

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:57.240
to remove yourself from the situation

00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:59.240
before something escalates and choose to

00:13:57.240 --> 00:14:01.360
walk away and leave a situation because

00:13:59.240 --> 00:14:03.760
you know what the future looks like if

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:05.360
you keep heading down this path and it's

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:07.800
not going to be good for anyone. Trust

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:09.960
me. Leaving takes more strength than

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:11.760
anything else, but if you can leave of

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:13.000
your own accord, that's only proof to

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:15.560
yourself that you can handle these

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:17.560
situations and you are tough. Standard

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:19.600
number five, I stopped being too

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:22.200
available. These days, I'm really

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:24.760
running on my own time and the Stoics

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:27.400
were obsessive about time. Seneca wrote

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:29.360
an entire essay called on the shortness

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:31.440
of life, where he says most people are

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:33.800
not living, they're just busy being

00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:36.720
available for other people's agendas. We

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:39.360
only have so much time in the world and

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:41.680
tomorrow is never guaranteed. So, why

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:43.480
are we constantly bending over to other

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:44.800
people's wills? I used to say yes to

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:46.600
things even though I didn't really want

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:48.240
to do it or arrange my whole day just to

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:49.880
meet someone else's needs. So, is that

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:51.280
really what having it all together

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:52.480
really looks like when you drop

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:54.160
everything just to put out someone

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:56.760
else's fire? Would those people do the

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:58.240
same thing for you? Honestly, I really

00:14:56.760 --> 00:14:59.920
don't think so. Instead of being

00:14:58.240 --> 00:15:01.480
reliable for other people, I started

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:03.120
being reliable for myself. So, my new

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:05.200
standard is I respond to people when I'm

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:06.640
ready to respond instead of saying, "Oh,

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:08.120
yes, of course we can do that. I can do

00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:10.040
that." Like I'll say, "Let me get back

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:11.600
to you on that." I start to also protect

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:13.520
my schedule as well, just like how I

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:14.839
protect my peace. And it is a wider part

00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:16.400
of protecting our boundaries because

00:15:14.839 --> 00:15:18.080
honestly, who is constantly available

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:19.960
all the time? People who have nothing

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:21.480
else going on in their lives and I don't

00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:22.720
think that's you, by the way. Especially

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:25.040
if you're someone who regularly watches

00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:26.880
my channel, I have interacted with many

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:28.640
of you. I have even met some of you,

00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:30.040
gone on vacations with some of you, on

00:15:28.640 --> 00:15:32.000
the group trip, that is. If you want to

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:34.200
do that, sign up for July. Anyways, my

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:36.120
core audience is incredibly smart, and I

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:37.600
have met a lot of people. A lot of them

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:39.240
have multiple degrees in higher

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:41.080
education, just like me, or they're

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:42.720
going to med school, they're Ivy League

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:44.080
educated, running their own business,

00:15:42.720 --> 00:15:46.600
they're high up in the food chain at

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:48.360
work. Doctors, engineers, executives,

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:50.120
biologists, this is the caliber of

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:52.680
audience I attract. Highly ambitious

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:54.120
people, or people who have figured their

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:55.760
life out, and they just live life as

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:57.480
they please. And I know for a fact that

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:58.880
you have things that you're working on,

00:15:57.480 --> 00:16:01.040
goals that you're building, you're

00:15:58.880 --> 00:16:03.240
designing your life consciously. If you

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:04.800
don't see it, I literally see that in

00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:06.920
you guys, so it's not even worth your

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:08.840
time to drop everything just to cater to

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:09.960
someone else's emergency. When you do

00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:11.360
that, you're basically saying to

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:13.600
yourself that your own work doesn't

00:16:11.360 --> 00:16:15.720
matter, and I can see for a fact for so

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:17.680
many of you, your work and your opinions

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:19.560
truly does matter. It's more important

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:21.680
than mine, sometimes, literally, like,

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:23.800
please, see yourself for your worth, and

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:25.520
treat yourself accordingly. I'm just

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:26.839
saying that I'm not quantifying worth or

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:28.400
anything, because I also don't believe

00:16:26.839 --> 00:16:29.960
in that, but if it's someone else's

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:31.400
mess, let them sort it out for

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:33.160
themselves. The only kind of people who

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:34.600
get frustrated at you protecting your

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:36.280
time and your boundaries are the people

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:37.800
who are already used to having unlimited

00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:39.760
access to you. Trust me when I say that

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:41.640
is not a real relationship, either.

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:43.440
Standard number six, I stopped trying to

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:45.480
fix people, and this is the observer

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:46.880
standard where everything converges into

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:49.960
this, because I used to come across

00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:52.240
people behaving badly, I would try to

00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:53.320
understand them, and explain to them,

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:54.600
like, "No, you're not doing this

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:55.640
correctly, like, there's a better way to

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:57.360
go about things." And I would try and

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:58.640
fix them. Maybe they're going through

00:16:57.360 --> 00:17:00.720
something, or maybe they don't realize

00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:02.240
how they're coming across. If I explain

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:03.760
how they are affecting me, maybe they'll

00:17:02.240 --> 00:17:05.319
change. Maybe some of these things might

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:06.839
even be true, they may be struggling

00:17:05.319 --> 00:17:08.600
with something that I don't know about,

00:17:06.839 --> 00:17:10.439
maybe they don't have any idea how they

00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:12.240
are coming across. Here's something I

00:17:10.439 --> 00:17:13.880
learned, and also a big reason why I

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:15.720
started this channel, to help only the

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:17.600
people who want to be helped, and it's

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:19.079
literally a recurring lesson from me. I

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:21.400
had to learn this over and over again.

00:17:19.079 --> 00:17:23.560
Some people are so wrapped up in their

00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:25.199
heads that your opinions don't even

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:27.640
matter to them in a way where they can't

00:17:25.199 --> 00:17:29.360
even take feedback at all. It's not like

00:17:27.640 --> 00:17:31.520
they can't see it, but seeing it will

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:33.920
require them to admit that they're doing

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:36.400
something wrong and they need to change.

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:38.800
Now, change is a very uncomfortable

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:41.360
concept for a lot of people. They may

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:43.400
even rather hurt you because it's easier

00:17:41.360 --> 00:17:45.320
to do that than to change. There are

00:17:43.400 --> 00:17:47.160
people who also genuinely believe that

00:17:45.320 --> 00:17:48.840
the world revolves around them and only

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:50.120
them. Not in like a we're all main

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:51.960
characters kind of way because

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:53.760
technically we are, but literally there

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:55.520
are narcissists out there where they

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:57.720
believe everyone else around them are

00:17:55.520 --> 00:17:59.640
just toys for them to play around with.

00:17:57.720 --> 00:18:01.840
They will deny any kind of wrongdoings

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:04.320
and darvo you. Darvo means to attack,

00:18:01.840 --> 00:18:06.640
reverse victim and offender. Meaning in

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:08.440
whatever situation, they're the victim

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:10.160
and you are the one to blame. Or they

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:11.880
will integrate it negatively where they

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:13.680
think that, "Oh, being mean is kind of

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:15.600
like a cute personality quirk." But

00:18:13.680 --> 00:18:17.080
low-key, they're really just bullies.

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:19.040
That's the thing about dark triad

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:20.720
personalities. They always will try to

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:22.280
find ways to make themselves look good.

00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:23.760
And I knew quite a few people like that,

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:25.400
but it didn't quite register to me at

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:27.480
the time because I didn't have the

00:18:25.400 --> 00:18:29.360
capacity to realize the things that I do

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:31.800
today. And you have to know that some

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:33.320
people have never been told no. Nobody

00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:35.280
has ever called them out and when they

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:36.800
do, these people will do literally

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:38.560
anything they can to deny it. And they

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:41.160
basically settle into this belief that

00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:43.840
they can do no wrong. The move for us is

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:46.680
to see that for what it is and observe

00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:48.040
it, name it for ourselves. Don't tell

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:49.900
them because they'll try to make you

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:51.800
look bad for doing that. You may think

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:54.240
[music] that you're doing them a favor,

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:55.760
but they cannot be saved. Their business

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:57.480
is not our problem. That's their work,

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:58.880
it's not yours. So just observe and

00:18:57.480 --> 00:19:01.680
protect yourself. If you have to

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:03.160
stonewall them, try to stay away from

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:05.120
them. If they're still determined to

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:07.600
repeat the patterns that hurt you and

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:09.520
try to hurt you again, remove yourself

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:11.840
or plan to remove yourself because being

00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:14.640
the observer is always more powerful

